SSO wave 1 live capture: silent server-completed consent landing
================================================================

Substrate: full local stack on the dev box (self-hosted GoTrue v2.189.0,
PostgREST, storage behind caddy-supabase; control-plane, edge-api,
web-console-prod built FROM THIS BRANCH behind caddy-console; Open WebUI
behind caddy-owui). Real OAuth 2.1 authorization-code round trips only;
no session injected, nothing stubbed. Sessions minted through the audited
one-time-token flow (tests/e2e/support/live-auth.mjs); no password was
set, read, reset or rotated for any account.

Every URL in this log has query strings AND fragments stripped before
commit; the same redaction is burned into the screenshot banners.

1. BEFORE (tracer baseline, team-lead 2026-08-23): repeat sign-in cost
   3 HTML loads plus 3 redirects, and the /oauth/consent stop painted
   "Checking your authorization request..." plus the Approve/Deny panel
   even when an auth.oauth_consents row already existed.

2. AFTER: repeat second-surface entry with ONLY the console ssr session
   (chat cookies and localStorage wiped first). Main-frame chain:

     200 http://localhost:3003/
     302 http://localhost:3003/oauth/oidc/login
     302 http://console.hive.test/auth/v1/oauth/authorize
     307 http://console.hive.test/oauth/consent        <- zero paint
     307 http://localhost:3003/oauth/oidc/callback
     200 http://localhost:3003/auth                    <- pass-through
     200 http://localhost:3003/
     FINAL http://localhost:3003/ (signed in)

   Consent landing answered 307: zero painted documents, zero Approve or
   Deny buttons ever rendered, zero password inputs. One redirect beyond
   the authorize round trip (the landing's own hand-off to the registered
   callback).

3. First-ever consent for a fresh user still paints the interactive panel
   exactly once; Approve completes into chat (frame captured:
   02-after-first-consent-panel-still-works.png). Wave 1 did not break
   the genuine approve/deny case.

